  "notes": [
    "The current project source bundle contains no Fanny Skill 1/death, Lancelot death, Aldous basic/Skill 1/Skill 2/death, or Gusion selection/movement/death assets. This pass maps the assets already bundled for those heroes and adds the requested Karrie Hawkwatch files; it does not claim those other assets are absent from every Fandom skin/page. No replacement voice lines were fabricated; existing action SFX remain intact.",
    "Idle/selection, movement/run, and death lines are now triggered through native passive lifecycle callbacks. TFM2 does not expose a dedicated pre-match hero-selection screen callback, so the selection line is played on champion spawn and reused as an occasional stationary idle bark.",
    "Movement/run barks are sampled from position changes and throttled to one line per 8 seconds; idle barks wait 12 seconds and then repeat no more often than every 20 seconds. These timings are mod-side heuristics and still require in-game verification.",
    "Estes Skill 1 and Skill 2 share the available generic skill voice; Lancelot Skill 1 and Skill 2 use the available basic exertion recordings because no dedicated skill lines are listed. These are deliberate existing-clip mappings, not invented recordings.",
    "Karrie Hawkwatch source OGG files are from the user-provided Fandom page and retained in source/audio/karrie_hawkwatch. The two Hawkwatch Ultimate clips are sequenced in the Ultimate sound event.",
    "All event IDs and clip IDs are independently routed through mod.override_info; static checks validate paths and bindings, but audio playback has not been tested inside TFM2.",
    "In v1.1.25, voice playback is routed through the shared native audio helper: a 5-second per-champion gate plus a sim-wide voice lock matched to each bundled clip duration. Routine voice attempts are dropped while busy; Ultimate/death priority lines are queued until the channel clears. Voice .sound_info volume multipliers are 0.68; these gates and levels need an in-game listening check.",
    "Custom action SFX are routed through short per-clip/per-champion duplicate suppression (15 ticks / 0.25 seconds). Aldous action SFX use 0.65 volume; quieter Gusion SFX remain unchanged. The generic Fanny SFX use the same short duplicate gate."
  ]
